1
00:02:46,767 --> 00:02:49,407
Yes, ma'am,
how ya doin'?

2
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,780
Is this Rose Hill?

3
00:02:51,839 --> 00:02:54,410
Good,
This is Ed Couch.

4
00:02:54,475 --> 00:02:56,921
I'm Vesta Adcock's nephew.

5
00:02:56,978 --> 00:02:59,219
I need to get up there
and see her,

6
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:03,285
but I'm gonna be late
'cause I'm lost out here.

7
00:03:03,351 --> 00:03:05,831
We're off the Alabama interstate
but I don't know where.

8
00:03:42,256 --> 00:03:46,170
- Did you hear that?
- What?

9
00:03:46,227 --> 00:03:48,298
The train.

10
00:03:48,362 --> 00:03:51,241
No, I didn't hear
no train.

11
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,344
Oh, nothin',
I guess.

12
00:03:55,403 --> 00:03:59,818
- Where's "Whistle Stop"
on the map?
- I can't find it.

13
00:03:59,874 --> 00:04:03,754
Why did you tell me to
turn right 10 miles back there?

14
00:04:05,279 --> 00:04:08,817
God, you got a negative
sense of direction, hon.

15
00:04:08,883 --> 00:04:11,762
I'm sorry.

16
00:04:11,819 --> 00:04:16,029
Oh, Ed,your aunt's gonna be
so disappointed we're late.

17
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:20,095
I know she's
been looking forward to
this visit all week long.

18
00:04:20,161 --> 00:04:23,438
Bless her sweet,
little ol' heart.

19
00:04:27,568 --> 00:04:30,447
Hey, how's my sweet Auntie V
this afternoon?

20
00:04:30,504 --> 00:04:33,110
Remember us?

21
00:04:33,174 --> 00:04:36,246
- Don't you look pretty!
- We brought you something.

22
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:39,484
- Let me look at you.

23
00:04:39,547 --> 00:04:42,153
Don't you know
Evelyn loves you?

24
00:04:42,216 --> 00:04:47,063
Well, honey,
I guess it'd be better if
you wait out here for me.

25
00:04:47,121 --> 00:04:51,592
-I'll get all this stuff.
- Well, if you think it's best.

26
00:04:51,659 --> 00:04:54,970
Yeah, I do this time.
Okay?

27
00:04:55,029 --> 00:04:57,202
Have a nice day,
Aunt Vesta.

28
00:04:57,265 --> 00:04:59,211
Don't you pitch a fit
like that'

29
00:05:11,178 --> 00:05:13,886
Did you know
they took my gallbladder out?

30
00:05:15,316 --> 00:05:17,455
No, I didn't.

31
00:05:17,518 --> 00:05:21,193
Oh, yes. Still
in the hospital in ajar.

32
00:05:21,255 --> 00:05:26,068
I guess that's where
they keep 'em.

33
00:05:26,127 --> 00:05:28,107
I guess.

34
00:05:28,162 --> 00:05:30,403
When I was
in the hospital,

35
00:05:30,464 --> 00:05:34,435
the nurse gave me one of them
Fleet enemas they're so fond of.

36
00:05:34,502 --> 00:05:37,108
Mrs. Cleo Threadgoode,

37
00:05:37,171 --> 00:05:40,482
82 year old widow,
imagine that.

38
00:05:40,541 --> 00:05:43,681
Actually,
everybody calls me Ninny.

39
00:05:43,744 --> 00:05:45,985
'Course I'm
just visitin' here.

40
00:05:46,047 --> 00:05:51,326
Did you ever have
one of them Fleet enemas?

41
00:05:51,385 --> 00:05:53,331
Um,well?

42
00:05:53,387 --> 00:05:55,458
No.

43
00:05:55,523 --> 00:05:58,766
You'd remember it.

44
00:05:58,826 --> 00:06:02,501
Me and my friend, Mrs. Otis,
come from Whistle Stop.

45
00:06:02,563 --> 00:06:04,770
You ever been
to Whistle Stop?

46
00:06:04,832 --> 00:06:08,245
Why, yes. I just
passed by there today.

47
00:06:08,302 --> 00:06:13,183
She's lived
down the street from me
for 30 years or more.

48
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,242
After her son died,

49
00:06:15,309 --> 00:06:18,916
her daughter-in-law had a fit
for her to come live
at the nursing home.

50
00:06:18,979 --> 00:06:22,290
They asked me to come
and be her roommate.

51
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:26,594
Mrs. Otis don't know it,
but I'm going home just soon
as she gets settled in good.

52
00:06:28,923 --> 00:06:32,336
Does the name
"Idgie Threadgoode"
ring a bell?

53
00:06:32,393 --> 00:06:35,931
Um, no, ma'am.
I don't think so.

54
00:06:35,996 --> 00:06:38,806
You'd remember her.

55
00:06:38,866 --> 00:06:42,780
You see,
I was practically adopted
by the Threadgoode family.

56
00:06:42,837 --> 00:06:45,181
- I married her brother, Cleo.
- Oh, uh-huh.

57
00:06:45,239 --> 00:06:50,018
Idgie and her friend Ruth,
ran the Whistle Stop Cafe.

58
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:52,023
Oh.

59
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:54,787
Idgie was a character,
all right.

60
00:06:54,849 --> 00:06:58,194
But how anybody
could've thought...

61
00:06:58,252 --> 00:07:02,291
she murdered that man
is beyond me.

62
00:07:02,356 --> 00:07:04,336
I beg your pardon?

63
00:07:04,392 --> 00:07:07,965
You sit and relax a while.
I'll tell you all about it.

64
00:07:08,028 --> 00:07:10,668
Oh, now, let's see.

65
00:07:10,731 --> 00:07:14,201
I 'member the day they pulled
that truck up out of the river.

66
00:07:15,875 --> 00:07:20,824
Idgie was Buddy's pet
from the day she was born.

67
00:07:23,216 --> 00:07:26,993
I 'member the day we
was all gettin' ready
for Leona's weddin'.

68
00:07:27,053 --> 00:07:29,033
The war had just ended,

69
00:07:29,088 --> 00:07:31,432
the Great one,
you know.

70
00:07:31,491 --> 00:07:36,167
And another one
was about to begin in
the Threadgoode house.

71
00:07:36,229 --> 00:07:38,675
Sipsey hone )4
is that finished?

72
00:07:40,233 --> 00:07:43,180
- Buddy,
get dressed honey.
- Mama?

73
00:07:43,236 --> 00:07:45,216
Leona, what is it?

74
00:07:45,271 --> 00:07:47,148
Idgie's upstairs
in her room...

75
00:07:47,207 --> 00:07:49,187
and says she won't come out
as long as she lives.

76
00:07:49,242 --> 00:07:51,381
- She is gonna ruin my weddin'!
- Shh.

77
00:07:51,444 --> 00:07:54,254
Leona, you're gonna be
the most beautiful bride.

78
00:07:54,314 --> 00:07:57,591
Of course she is, Papa.

79
00:07:57,650 --> 00:08:01,598
Your papa has spent
every last nickel he has
just to make you happy.

80
00:08:01,654 --> 00:08:05,466
Now, you try to act
a little grateful, young lady.

81
00:08:05,525 --> 00:08:08,631
Imogene Louise Threadgoode!

82
00:08:08,695 --> 00:08:11,232
This is your mama!

83
00:08:13,633 --> 00:08:18,582
You come down here right now.
Do you hear me?

84
00:08:18,638 --> 00:08:21,278
- Buddy, fetch her.
She'll listen to you.
- Come on down, little bit.

85
00:08:21,341 --> 00:08:23,912
There's no firin'
squad waitin' for you.

86
00:08:23,977 --> 00:08:29,325
Ohh! Come on, honey
Let us see you.

87
00:08:29,382 --> 00:08:31,555
You look so pretty.

88
00:08:31,618 --> 00:08:34,462
- I see London,
I see-
- Hush!

89
00:08:36,189 --> 00:08:39,636
Julian, hush.

90
00:08:39,692 --> 00:08:42,434
Come ahead, sweetheart.

91
00:08:42,495 --> 00:08:46,238
You look awful nice
in that.

92
00:08:46,299 --> 00:08:47,903
- Mama!
- You look fine.

93
00:08:47,967 --> 00:08:50,470
She looks like a monkey

94
00:08:50,537 --> 00:08:52,346
Julian, stop it
right this second!

95
00:08:52,405 --> 00:08:55,750
Take it back!
Take it back!
Idgie, hey!

96
00:08:55,808 --> 00:08:58,914
I told you she
was gonna ruin my weddin'!

97
00:08:58,978 --> 00:09:01,356
- Idgie, get up.
- Take it back!

98
00:09:01,414 --> 00:09:03,587
Take it back!

99
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:06,995
- I'll get you for this.
- No, Buddy.

100
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:13,862
We have to be careful
when she's dressing up.

101
00:09:13,927 --> 00:09:15,873
She's just a pain!

102
00:09:15,929 --> 00:09:19,467
Leona, will you
stop shrieking'

103
00:09:19,532 --> 00:09:22,240
This is your
weddin ' day'

104
00:09:33,246 --> 00:09:36,090
I oaks like you got yourself
up a tree, little bit.

105
00:09:36,149 --> 00:09:39,187
I'm sick of people
makin' fun of me.

106
00:09:39,252 --> 00:09:41,789
So you're gonna stay up here
all day long.

107
00:09:41,854 --> 00:09:45,063
Yep.
The hell with them.

108
00:09:45,124 --> 00:09:49,072
Who wants to wear
that stupid ol' dress anyway?

109
00:09:49,128 --> 00:09:52,507
- I ever tell you about the oysters?
- Oysters?

110
00:09:52,565 --> 00:09:54,511
- I tell you about the oysters?
- No.

111
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:59,243
Think about the millions of
oysters lyin' around the ocean.

112
00:09:59,305 --> 00:10:01,649
Then one day...

113
00:10:01,708 --> 00:10:04,518
God comes along and sees one
and he says,

114
00:10:04,577 --> 00:10:07,490
"I think I'm gonna make
that one different."

115
00:10:07,547 --> 00:10:09,754
You know what he does?

116
00:10:09,816 --> 00:10:12,990
He puts a little
piece of sand in it.

117
00:10:13,052 --> 00:10:17,296
- Guess what it can do
that the others can't.
- What?

118
00:10:17,357 --> 00:10:20,668
It can make
a beautiful pearl.

119
00:10:20,727 --> 00:10:22,900
What if God
made a mistake?

120
00:10:22,962 --> 00:10:28,071
Well, the way I figure it,
he never makes mistakes.

121
00:10:28,134 --> 00:10:30,910
I mean, he made sure
we got together.

122
00:10:30,970 --> 00:10:32,972
He made sure you got
the best looking,

123
00:10:33,039 --> 00:10:35,246
most charmin' brother
in the world...

124
00:10:35,308 --> 00:10:38,687
- who's gonna beat you
to the chocolate cake.
- You will not.

125
00:10:38,745 --> 00:10:41,123
Got you out of the tree,
didn't I?

126
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:44,127
Did not!

127
00:10:44,183 --> 00:10:47,824
Into this estate,
these two come now to be joined

128
00:10:47,887 --> 00:10:49,992
If any man present
can show cause...

129
00:10:50,056 --> 00:10:52,468
why they may not lawfully
be joined together,

130
00:10:52,525 --> 00:10:57,668
let him speak now or
forever after hold his peace.

131
00:10:57,730 --> 00:11:00,404
Please be seated.

132
00:11:02,769 --> 00:11:04,976
If either of you
know any reason...

133
00:11:05,038 --> 00:11:08,019
why you may not justly
be joined together
in holy matrimony

134
00:11:08,074 --> 00:11:10,554
do you now confess it?

135
00:11:20,186 --> 00:11:22,894
It is then your will
to proceed.

136
00:11:22,955 --> 00:11:26,664
Do you,
Charles Osgood justice-

137
00:11:32,498 --> 00:11:35,843
Thank you. I don't know what
we'd do without your generosity.

138
00:11:35,902 --> 00:11:38,883
Sipsey, especially you.
Look what you've clone!

139
00:11:38,938 --> 00:11:42,886
Thank you, Mrs. Threadgoode.
Gimme that, you rascal!

140
00:11:47,213 --> 00:11:49,784
John!
Jump on my back

141
00:11:49,849 --> 00:11:53,490
I don't think
there ever was a sweeter boy
than Buddy Threadgoode.

142
00:11:53,553 --> 00:11:58,059
- You look beautiful, Lily.
- Yes, Lily, you sure do.

143
00:11:58,124 --> 00:12:01,571
I had the biggest crush
on him.

144
00:12:01,627 --> 00:12:03,971
He was a terrible flirt!

145
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:07,273
But his heart belonged
to Ruth Jamison.

146
00:12:07,333 --> 00:12:10,507
She was the daughter of
a friend of his mama's...

147
00:12:10,570 --> 00:12:13,380
who was visitin'
that summer.

148
00:12:13,439 --> 00:12:16,909
Ruth Jamison,
you're just the one
I've been lookin' for.

149
00:12:16,976 --> 00:12:20,082
- Are you thirsty?
- Let's go visit
someplace else.

150
00:12:25,985 --> 00:12:29,330
Think that's a big lake,
you should've seen the
one next to our house.

151
00:12:29,388 --> 00:12:31,527
We used to swim in it
and fish.

152
00:12:31,591 --> 00:12:34,265
I sure do miss it.
Sure do.

153
00:12:34,327 --> 00:12:37,069
What happened to it?
Did it dry up?

154
00:12:37,130 --> 00:12:39,076
No, worse than that.

155
00:12:39,132 --> 00:12:41,203
Last fall,
a ﬂock of ducks,

156
00:12:41,267 --> 00:12:45,545
40 or 50 of 'em,
landed right smack
in the middle of it.

157
00:12:45,605 --> 00:12:47,482
This ﬂuke thing
happened.

158
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:50,020
The temperature dropped so fast
that the whole lake froze...

159
00:12:50,076 --> 00:12:52,078
in three seconds,
just like that!

160
00:12:52,145 --> 00:12:54,455
Those poor little ducks.
Did it kill them?

161
00:12:54,514 --> 00:12:57,723
No, they ﬂew off
and took the lake with 'em.

162
00:12:57,784 --> 00:13:01,163
To this very day, that lake
is somewhere over in Georgia.

163
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:04,667
Buddy Threadgoode.

164
00:13:15,635 --> 00:13:18,980
Come a little closer.
I wanna give you something.

165
00:13:19,038 --> 00:13:21,484
Come here.

166
00:13:25,344 --> 00:13:27,585
Whoop!

167
00:13:31,717 --> 00:13:35,130
Come back here, hat. Where
do you think you're gain'?

168
00:13:37,356 --> 00:13:39,302
Whoa!

169
00:13:39,358 --> 00:13:42,464
I got it.
Hold on, Ruth.
Hold on, little bit.

170
00:13:46,866 --> 00:13:49,608
It's all right.
I got it.

171
00:13:51,737 --> 00:13:55,480
Come here,
you damn hat.
Got it!

172
00:13:55,541 --> 00:13:58,488
Oh, I meant
to do that.

173
00:13:59,545 --> 00:14:03,288
I... got it!

174
00:14:03,349 --> 00:14:05,226
Ta-da!

175
00:14:07,019 --> 00:14:09,556
All right.
Damn!

176
00:14:09,622 --> 00:14:11,602
Come on.

177
00:14:18,231 --> 00:14:23,112
Come on. Get out.
Get out.

178
00:14:23,169 --> 00:14:25,115
Buddy!

179
00:14:25,171 --> 00:14:28,414
- Buddy!
- Buddy Threadgoode!

180
00:14:30,042 --> 00:14:31,749
Come on, Buddy!

181
00:14:31,811 --> 00:14:33,552
Get out.

182
00:14:35,014 --> 00:14:37,153
Get out of there.

183
00:14:38,484 --> 00:14:42,296
Buddy!

184
00:14:42,355 --> 00:14:45,495
- Come on, Buddy!
- Buddy'

185
00:14:45,558 --> 00:14:48,164
Buddy!

186
00:14:50,696 --> 00:14:53,302
No-o-o!

187
00:14:53,366 --> 00:14:57,212
Buddy!

188
00:14:57,270 --> 00:15:00,683
Buddy, no!
No!

189
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:03,516
No! Buddy!
No-o-o!

190
00:15:03,576 --> 00:15:06,614
No! Buddy!
Let me go!

191
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:11,892
' No!
- Buddy!

192
00:15:11,951 --> 00:15:15,592
- You got to go back to the house.

193
00:15:15,655 --> 00:15:18,158
Come on.
We're gonna go home.

194
00:15:18,224 --> 00:15:21,068
- Buddy!
- You have to be strong.

195
00:15:21,127 --> 00:15:24,040
- It'll be okay.
- Buddy!

196
00:15:24,096 --> 00:15:27,043
"The Lord is my Shepherd,

197
00:15:27,099 --> 00:15:29,306
I shall not want."

198
00:15:29,368 --> 00:15:32,372
Oh, it like
to have killed us all

199
00:15:32,438 --> 00:15:35,112
But nary a one took it
as hard as Idgie,

200
00:15:38,210 --> 00:15:43,683
everyone thought she 'o' die
right along with him.

201
00:16:00,333 --> 00:16:04,611
Night alter night,
she stayed by the river.

202
00:16:04,670 --> 00:16:08,846
Big George was the only soul
she'd let near her,

203
00:16:08,908 --> 00:16:12,446
and he watched over her
night and day

204
00:16:12,511 --> 00:16:15,321
You know,
a heart can be broken,

205
00:16:15,381 --> 00:16:18,453
but it still keeps a-beatin'
just the same.

206
00:16:18,517 --> 00:16:21,157
Miss Idgie, you'll have
to keep this blanket on...

207
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:24,133
or you'll catch
your death of cold,
you hear me now?

208
00:16:24,190 --> 00:16:28,605
That's so sad.

209
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,606
Ah.

210
00:16:36,669 --> 00:16:38,671
Would you like
one of these?

211
00:16:38,738 --> 00:16:40,740
Oh, thank ya,
honey.

212
00:16:40,806 --> 00:16:42,683
Evelyn?

213
00:16:42,742 --> 00:16:44,915
Honey,
we gotta get goin'.

214
00:16:44,977 --> 00:16:47,389
The Braves' game's
fixin' to start...

215
00:16:47,446 --> 00:16:49,084
and you're gonna miss
your... thing.

216
00:16:49,148 --> 00:16:52,891
Excuse me.
That's my husband, Ed.

217
00:16:52,952 --> 00:16:55,023
Hi, ma'am.
How you doin'?

218
00:16:55,087 --> 00:16:58,534
Um.

219
00:16:58,591 --> 00:17:00,662
I can't believe
Buddy died.

220
00:17:00,726 --> 00:17:03,332
Neither could I.

221
00:17:03,396 --> 00:17:06,809
Oh, well, I enjoyed
talkin' to you, honey.

222
00:17:06,866 --> 00:17:08,868
What's your name?

223
00:17:08,934 --> 00:17:12,006
Evelyn...
Evelyn Couch.

224
00:17:12,071 --> 00:17:16,850
- I've got to go.
- You come back and see me,
you hear?

225
00:17:16,909 --> 00:17:20,823
- Okay.
- Bye-bye.

226
00:17:21,013 --> 00:17:23,289
First of all,
I want you...

227
00:17:23,349 --> 00:17:25,955
to truly
dedicate yourselves...

228
00:17:26,018 --> 00:17:30,057
to finding little ways
to putting that magic,
that spark...

229
00:17:30,122 --> 00:17:32,329
back into your marriage.

230
00:17:32,391 --> 00:17:36,339
When we think of
romance and marriage,

231
00:17:36,395 --> 00:17:40,434
- what is the first thought
that comes into your mind?
- Divorce!

232
00:17:40,499 --> 00:17:44,208
Remember when counselors
used to tell you to wrap
yourself in cellophane...

233
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:46,477
to put a little charge
into your marriage?

234
00:17:46,539 --> 00:17:49,349
Do we really pay
for these lectures?

235
00:17:49,408 --> 00:17:52,116
You can see,
it is truly up to you...

236
00:17:52,178 --> 00:17:55,682
to put romance back
into your relationship.

237
00:18:23,375 --> 00:18:25,355
Evelyn,
have you gone insane?

238
00:18:25,411 --> 00:18:27,357
My God
people can see you!

239
00:18:27,413 --> 00:18:29,484
What if I had been
the paperboy?

240
00:18:29,548 --> 00:18:31,323
Get in there!

241
00:18:31,383 --> 00:18:34,193
What are you
thinking about?

242
00:18:34,987 --> 00:18:38,332
Evelyn?

243
00:18:38,390 --> 00:18:40,700
- Evelyn!
- Oh.

244
00:18:40,759 --> 00:18:44,730
You know, what we really need
instead of this baloney...

245
00:18:44,797 --> 00:18:48,870
is an assertiveness
training class for
Southern women.

246
00:18:48,934 --> 00:18:52,507
But that's a contradiction
in terms, isn't it?

247
00:18:52,571 --> 00:18:55,814
Especially you, sweetheart.
You're livin' in the Dark Ages.

248
00:19:19,064 --> 00:19:21,670
- Hi, honey.
I need one of those.
- Hi!

249
00:19:21,734 --> 00:19:24,510
Mmm, you smell good too.

250
00:19:24,570 --> 00:19:26,607
I need one of these.

251
00:19:26,672 --> 00:19:29,619
- Oh, this looks good!
- Uh-huh.

252
00:19:29,675 --> 00:19:31,621
Yes, indeedy.

253
00:19:40,786 --> 00:19:43,767
Ed.

254
00:19:45,457 --> 00:19:47,630
Why don't you come in?
and sit down at the table...

255
00:19:47,693 --> 00:19:51,641
- and have dinner with me?
- I'm sorry.
The game's almost over.

256
00:19:51,697 --> 00:19:54,541
I just want to see
a little bit of it.
Why you so dressed up?

257
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:57,103
Honey, don't get in the way.
Scoot over a bit.

258
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,810
Ed?

259
00:20:02,875 --> 00:20:05,879
If I'd answered the door
wearing only cellophane,

260
00:20:05,945 --> 00:20:09,256
would you still be
watching the baseball game?

261
00:20:09,315 --> 00:20:13,058
No, honey. I'd probably
be checking you into
a looney bin.

262
00:20:35,374 --> 00:20:39,618
Hi, sugar.

263
00:20:39,678 --> 00:20:41,624
- How's my dumplin'?
- Trick or treat!

264
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:43,626
You 're not gonna throw
them hissy-fits, are you?

265
00:20:43,682 --> 00:20:46,925
Happy Halloween!
Oh, no. No, no, no!

266
00:20:46,986 --> 00:20:49,091
You 're meaner
than a damn snake.

267
00:20:49,154 --> 00:20:51,156
I'm glad
you're feeling better.

268
00:20:51,223 --> 00:20:54,466
- Get back in bed
- Good thing
your eyesight's failing.

269
00:21:04,103 --> 00:21:07,243
- Hey!
- Mmm. Oh.

270
00:21:07,306 --> 00:21:10,719
- Hey.
- I was hopin'
you'd be here.

271
00:21:10,776 --> 00:21:14,849
My roommate, Mrs. Otis,
said I could visit her family,

272
00:21:14,913 --> 00:21:16,859
but I said,
"Thank you kindly,

273
00:21:16,915 --> 00:21:19,555
but I think I might have
my own visitor."

274
00:21:19,618 --> 00:21:21,620
And here you are.

275
00:21:21,687 --> 00:21:23,963
- Well, sit down.
- Thank you.

276
00:21:24,023 --> 00:21:27,561
And doughnuts to boot!
You can't beat that.

277
00:21:27,626 --> 00:21:30,470
- Well, help yourself,
Mrs. Threadgoode.
- Thank you.

278
00:21:31,196 --> 00:21:32,231
How's your friend?

279
00:21:32,298 --> 00:21:34,300
- Mrs. Otis?
- Uh-huh.

280
00:21:34,366 --> 00:21:37,313
- Well, not so good.
- Oh.

281
00:21:37,369 --> 00:21:40,111
Looks like I won't be
gettin' home for quite a while,

282
00:21:40,172 --> 00:21:43,619
and I sure miss it.

283
00:21:43,676 --> 00:21:46,953
Funny what you miss
when you're away from home.

284
00:21:47,012 --> 00:21:49,424
I miss
the smell of coffee...

285
00:21:49,481 --> 00:21:52,291
and bacon fryin'.

286
00:21:52,351 --> 00:21:56,857
Oh, what I wouldn't give for a
plate of fried green tomatoes...

287
00:21:56,922 --> 00:21:59,630
like we used to have
at the cafe.

288
00:21:59,692 --> 00:22:02,104
Ooh!

289
00:22:05,631 --> 00:22:08,703
I never told you
about the cafe,
did I?

290
00:22:08,767 --> 00:22:10,713
No, ma'am.

291
00:22:10,769 --> 00:22:15,377
Oh, well...
now let me back up a bit.

292
00:22:15,441 --> 00:22:20,686
You see, Idgie never
quite got over losing Buddy.

293
00:22:23,015 --> 00:22:26,087
She hardly
ever come home.

294
00:22:26,151 --> 00:22:29,030
Only Big George
knew how to find her.

295
00:22:29,088 --> 00:22:33,833
She just didn't seem to care
about anythin' anymore.

296
00:22:33,892 --> 00:22:35,838
Then, one summer day

297
00:22:39,743 --> 00:22:42,553
Come on in, honey.
She's right down here.

298
00:22:42,613 --> 00:22:46,060
- Here? Okay.
- Uh-huh.

299
00:22:46,116 --> 00:22:48,756
I'll see you,
Grady Kilgore,

300
00:22:48,819 --> 00:22:50,890
and I'll
raise you twenty.

301
00:22:50,954 --> 00:22:53,525
You ain't got nothin'!

302
00:22:53,590 --> 00:22:56,901
Maybe I do and
maybe I don't.

303
00:22:56,960 --> 00:23:01,204
Put your money where
your mouth is, Mr. Sheriff.

304
00:23:05,235 --> 00:23:07,875
Well, look what
the cat drug in!

305
00:23:07,938 --> 00:23:11,818
I came to talk to you.

306
00:23:11,875 --> 00:23:14,253
You're gonna have to wait.
I'm busy.

307
00:23:14,311 --> 00:23:16,917
Come on, Grady, this
is your big chance.
You in or out?

308
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:19,426
I'll make you
a rich man.

309
00:23:19,483 --> 00:23:22,487
You just bluffin' again
as usual

310
00:23:22,552 --> 00:23:25,556
I'm afraid you're gonna
have to excuse Idgie.
She's goin' home for dinner.

311
00:23:25,622 --> 00:23:27,795
- Say good-bye, Idgie.
- Where you goin'?

312
00:23:27,858 --> 00:23:32,238
- Where the hell you goin'
with my money?
- We're goin' home!

313
00:23:32,295 --> 00:23:36,243
- Who are you to boss me around?
- The one holdin' your money!

314
00:23:36,299 --> 00:23:38,245
Give it back.

315
00:23:38,301 --> 00:23:40,440
Now, get in the car.

316
00:23:42,305 --> 00:23:45,548
All right.
I'll get in the car.

317
00:23:45,609 --> 00:23:48,112
You win!

318
00:23:48,178 --> 00:23:51,159
Come on.

319
00:23:51,214 --> 00:23:52,784
Sucker!

320
00:23:52,849 --> 00:23:54,886
I'll leave when I want!

321
00:23:54,951 --> 00:23:58,763
I don't know how you can break
your mother's heart like you do.

322
00:23:58,822 --> 00:24:00,995
I'm not doin' anything
to my mother.

323
00:24:01,058 --> 00:24:03,629
Oh, no? Why do you think
I'm here for the summer?

324
00:24:03,694 --> 00:24:07,073
Your mother was so worried,
she thought I might be able
to talk some sense into you.

325
00:24:07,130 --> 00:24:09,474
But you're too busy
being selfish!

326
00:24:09,533 --> 00:24:12,514
What are you
talkin' about?

327
00:24:12,569 --> 00:24:16,278
You're not the only one
who lost Buddy.

328
00:24:16,339 --> 00:24:18,444
We all miss him...

329
00:24:18,508 --> 00:24:21,387
but turning your back on
your family is not gonna help.

330
00:24:23,747 --> 00:24:25,818
What's he got to do
with anything?

331
00:24:25,882 --> 00:24:30,024
I oaks like you 're
the one with the problem
forgetting my brother.

332
00:24:34,391 --> 00:24:36,894
Why just ten miles a way ..

333
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:38,871
Down by the river,

334
00:24:38,929 --> 00:24:41,170
there lurks
a den of the devil...

335
00:24:48,453 --> 00:24:51,730
Let's turn to page 53
in our hymnal.

336
00:24:57,829 --> 00:25:00,833
Yoo-hoo!

337
00:25:00,899 --> 00:25:05,712
Big George thought
I might find you here.

338
00:25:08,573 --> 00:25:13,420
If you give me a chance,
a chance to get to know you,

339
00:25:13,478 --> 00:25:17,221
maybe it'll be fun!

340
00:25:17,282 --> 00:25:20,695
Fun?

341
00:25:20,752 --> 00:25:24,029
Idgie,just spend
some time with me.

342
00:25:24,089 --> 00:25:26,035
Please?

343
00:25:26,091 --> 00:25:28,037
Suit yourself.

344
00:25:28,727 --> 00:25:31,401
You sure you don't
wanna back out?

345
00:25:31,463 --> 00:25:34,672
- It's not too late.
- I'm sure.

346
00:25:34,733 --> 00:25:37,077
Here, hold this.

347
00:25:39,070 --> 00:25:41,778
Tell me now,
you like trains?

348
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:45,652
- Yes.
- Good.

349
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:49,624
We'll get along
just fine!

350
00:25:51,116 --> 00:25:54,620
Boy, did we
luck out tonight.

351
00:25:57,489 --> 00:25:59,730
Hop in.

352
00:25:59,791 --> 00:26:02,328
Hop?

353
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:05,432
Oh. Give me
your hand.

354
00:26:05,497 --> 00:26:07,977
Put your foot
up there.

355
00:26:17,275 --> 00:26:19,414
Hold that.

356
00:26:20,311 --> 00:26:23,121
Ooo-ooo!
Look at all this!

357
00:26:27,719 --> 00:26:31,292
Don't you think we should
get off the train?
It's startin' to move.

358
00:26:31,356 --> 00:26:35,168
No. The fun
just started!

359
00:26:38,496 --> 00:26:40,908
You all right?

360
00:26:40,965 --> 00:26:45,209
Well, sometimes I get
a little dizzy lookin' down.

361
00:26:45,270 --> 00:26:47,978
Don't look down.

362
00:27:00,852 --> 00:27:04,629
- What are you doin'?
- Come on. Look.

363
00:27:04,689 --> 00:27:07,602
They're throwin'
away food!

364
00:27:11,429 --> 00:27:14,069
You talk about
"give unto others."

365
00:27:26,423 --> 00:27:28,061
- More!
- Give me some.

366
00:27:53,383 --> 00:27:56,762
Okay, time to get off.

367
00:27:57,387 --> 00:27:59,367
We gotta jump.

368
00:27:59,422 --> 00:28:02,028
Lump?

369
00:28:02,092 --> 00:28:05,164
Yeah jump. The next stop's
five miles down the tracks.

370
00:28:05,228 --> 00:28:07,230
I don't wanna walk
that far back.

371
00:28:07,297 --> 00:28:10,176
Are you crazy?

372
00:28:10,233 --> 00:28:12,611
You're not kiddin'.

373
00:28:12,669 --> 00:28:16,344
Well...

374
00:28:16,406 --> 00:28:18,886
I give up. Jump.-

375
00:28:18,942 --> 00:28:22,219
I'll tell Mama I'm not
a good influence on you-

376
00:28:22,279 --> 00:28:24,555
You'll never jump,
will you?

377
00:28:26,583 --> 00:28:29,723
Don't say "never"
to me.

378
00:28:41,765 --> 00:28:44,541
Towanda!

379
00:28:57,414 --> 00:29:00,020
- You all right?
- I'm fine.

380
00:29:00,083 --> 00:29:03,656
I'm all right.

381
00:29:03,720 --> 00:29:05,859
Ow!

382
00:29:05,922 --> 00:29:08,266
Does this hurt?

383
00:29:08,325 --> 00:29:11,101
Guess so.

384
00:29:11,161 --> 00:29:13,471
- We better get you
to a doc-doctor.
- Shit!

385
00:29:13,530 --> 00:29:15,635
Which way is it?

386
00:29:15,699 --> 00:29:19,306
About two miles
down the tracks.

387
00:29:19,369 --> 00:29:21,610
All right.
let's go.

388
00:29:23,406 --> 00:29:26,910
You'll never be able
to carry me that far.

389
00:29:26,977 --> 00:29:29,685
I know.
Never say never.

390
00:29:29,746 --> 00:29:33,888
I'm not carryin' you.
You're walkin'.

391
00:29:39,823 --> 00:29:44,568
Thank you, Julian.
I owe you one.

392
00:29:56,473 --> 00:29:58,419
Uh. Ow.

393
00:29:58,475 --> 00:30:02,048
Aren't you ready yet?

394
00:30:02,112 --> 00:30:04,217
What?

395
00:30:06,283 --> 00:30:09,355
This doesn't have anything
to do with trains, does it?

396
00:30:10,253 --> 00:30:12,494
You like honey?

397
00:30:12,555 --> 00:30:14,535
Yeah, I like honey.

398
00:30:14,591 --> 00:30:16,593
- Fresh honey?
- Yeah.

399
00:30:16,660 --> 00:30:20,198
Me too.
There it is.

400
00:30:20,263 --> 00:30:24,473
There what... is?

401
00:30:24,534 --> 00:30:28,414
You'll see soon enough.

402
00:30:32,375 --> 00:30:34,616
Now... stay here.

403
00:30:34,678 --> 00:30:37,625
No matter what happens,
don't move.

404
00:30:37,681 --> 00:30:40,958
What are you
gonna do?

405
00:31:15,952 --> 00:31:18,057
Ah.

406
00:31:52,655 --> 00:31:56,262
Here you are, madam.
This is for you.

407
00:31:56,326 --> 00:32:00,706
Why did you do that?
You could have been killed.

408
00:32:00,764 --> 00:32:04,268
I'm sorry.

409
00:32:04,334 --> 00:32:07,042
Don't you want
the honey?

410
00:32:07,103 --> 00:32:10,448
I got it
just for you.

411
00:32:10,507 --> 00:32:12,987
It's all right.
I do it all the time.

412
00:32:13,042 --> 00:32:16,819
I never get stung,
honest.

413
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:18,882
Don't be
mad at me, Ruth.

414
00:32:18,948 --> 00:32:22,862
Idgie.
I'm not mad at you.

415
00:32:22,919 --> 00:32:25,490
No foolin'?

416
00:32:32,295 --> 00:32:35,003
Is it bad,
what I did?

417
00:32:35,064 --> 00:32:37,408
No.

418
00:32:37,467 --> 00:32:39,640
I thought I might
be crazy or somethin'.

419
00:32:39,702 --> 00:32:42,512
No, no.

420
00:32:42,572 --> 00:32:46,247
I've heard there were people
who could charm bees.

421
00:32:46,309 --> 00:32:49,950
I've just never
seen it done...
before today.

422
00:32:51,848 --> 00:32:56,228
You're just a bee charmer,
Idgie Threadgoode.

423
00:32:56,286 --> 00:33:00,757
That's what you are,
a bee charmer.

424
00:33:00,824 --> 00:33:03,566
Here, you want
to taste it?

425
00:33:09,699 --> 00:33:12,441
"Satan started to laugh
at job's devotion.

426
00:33:12,502 --> 00:33:17,747
"He bet God that job would
never have so much faith...

427
00:33:17,807 --> 00:33:19,912
"if he didn't have
so many blessings.

428
00:33:19,976 --> 00:33:23,856
"He went on and on
so long and so much
that God finally agreed...

429
00:33:23,913 --> 00:33:26,621
"to let Satan
put Job to a test.

430
00:33:26,683 --> 00:33:29,823
"Suddenly from bein'
on top of the world,

431
00:33:29,886 --> 00:33:33,527
Job was plunged down
into the deepest pits
of misery."

432
00:33:35,558 --> 00:33:38,300
Surprise!

433
00:33:40,563 --> 00:33:42,509
Idgie Threadgoode!

434
00:33:42,565 --> 00:33:44,511
Tonight we're gonna have
a real party.

435
00:33:44,567 --> 00:33:46,808
Drink this... and then,
we're gonna play some poker.

436
00:33:46,870 --> 00:33:50,750
I don't know
how to play poker
and I never drink...

437
00:33:50,807 --> 00:33:52,809
but thank you anyway.

438
00:33:57,947 --> 00:34:00,450
Here comes the windup.

439
00:34:00,517 --> 00:34:02,861
Burn that ball in here.
Burn 'em in here!

440
00:34:02,919 --> 00:34:07,299
- Right in the pocket.
- I don't know how
to bat.

441
00:34:07,357 --> 00:34:10,167
And you don't drink,
either.

442
00:34:10,226 --> 00:34:13,332
- It's gonna be a spitter.
- Hold the bat and swing

443
00:34:13,396 --> 00:34:15,137
Spitter?

444
00:34:15,198 --> 00:34:18,407
- She gonna spit at me?
- She's gonna spit on the ball

445
00:34:18,468 --> 00:34:21,677
Swing that bat!
Take another crack at it.

446
00:34:21,738 --> 00:34:23,911
I'm gonna take
another crack at it.

447
00:34:23,973 --> 00:34:27,182
Get 'em in here.

448
00:34:34,684 --> 00:34:37,494
Now run, Ruth.
Run!

449
00:34:37,554 --> 00:34:39,556
Come on
around the bases!

450
00:34:39,622 --> 00:34:41,624
Don't kiss everybody.
Run!

451
00:34:41,691 --> 00:34:44,729
I have never had
so much fun...

452
00:34:44,794 --> 00:34:47,138
in my whole life.

453
00:34:47,196 --> 00:34:50,507
I even got a home run.

454
00:34:50,567 --> 00:34:53,548
A clean one
at that!

455
00:34:53,603 --> 00:34:56,812
A straight beats
three of a kind.

456
00:35:01,911 --> 00:35:06,155
You know,
poker isn't half bad.

457
00:35:06,215 --> 00:35:08,388
What's your mother
gonna say...

458
00:35:08,451 --> 00:35:11,830
when she sees us both...
drunk?

459
00:35:11,888 --> 00:35:15,802
- You gotta stop worrying
about what people think.
- I know.

460
00:35:15,858 --> 00:35:17,860
You've always done
the right thing.

461
00:35:17,927 --> 00:35:21,374
You took care of your daddy,
the preacher, when he took sick.

462
00:35:21,431 --> 00:35:25,311
You take care of all the kids
over at the church school.

463
00:35:25,368 --> 00:35:28,110
You're gonna
take care of your mama.

464
00:35:28,171 --> 00:35:31,709
And I'm gonna marry
the man I'm supposed to.

465
00:35:31,774 --> 00:35:34,050
You gettin' married?

466
00:35:34,110 --> 00:35:38,388
As soon as
the summer's over.

467
00:35:41,918 --> 00:35:45,627
Oh, am I
gonna miss you.

468
00:35:45,688 --> 00:35:48,828
This is
the best birthday...

469
00:35:48,891 --> 00:35:51,872
I ever had.

470
00:36:03,416 --> 00:36:06,659
No sir!
Whew!

471
00:36:06,720 --> 00:36:10,998
Now, Mama Jamison,
you put that down.

472
00:36:11,057 --> 00:36:13,663
Oh, my Lord!

473
00:36:20,166 --> 00:36:22,305
During these next few weeks,

474
00:36:22,369 --> 00:36:26,715
we will be learning to reclaim
our own power as women!

475
00:36:26,773 --> 00:36:28,878
Hallelujah!

476
00:36:28,942 --> 00:36:33,721
And tonight, we're gonna
begin to explore...

477
00:36:33,780 --> 00:36:35,987
our own femaleness...

478
00:36:36,049 --> 00:36:40,623
by examining the source
of our strength...

479
00:36:40,687 --> 00:36:43,065
and our separateness.

480
00:36:43,123 --> 00:36:45,103
Our vaginas.

481
00:36:47,060 --> 00:36:49,870
So if ya'll will just
slip off your panties...

482
00:36:49,929 --> 00:36:53,467
and straddle your mirrors.

483
00:36:53,533 --> 00:36:56,207
Ms. Couch!

484
00:36:56,269 --> 00:36:59,716
Ms. Couch!

485
00:36:59,773 --> 00:37:04,153
Um, I need to be excused
for a minute.

486
00:37:04,210 --> 00:37:08,283
Um, Missy, could you come
with me to the ladies' room?

487
00:37:08,348 --> 00:37:12,091
- Do you find this threatening?
- Uh, well, um-

488
00:37:12,152 --> 00:37:16,294
- do you have a problem
with your sexuality?
- No, ma'am.

489
00:37:16,356 --> 00:37:19,394
But I do have a problem
with my girdle.

490
00:37:44,150 --> 00:37:47,723
All right, fried chicken!
My favorite.

491
00:37:53,593 --> 00:37:55,732
Ed?

492
00:37:55,795 --> 00:37:58,867
Ed?

493
