729
00:55:48,204 --> 00:55:52,243
You shoulda seen that
big ox down by the river.

730
00:55:52,308 --> 00:55:56,347
Three solid days,
drunk as a dog,
cryin' like a baby...

731
00:55:56,412 --> 00:55:59,188
'cause Joe,
that ol' colored man
that raised him, died.

732
00:55:59,248 --> 00:56:01,194
- Remember that, Sipsey?
- Yes'm.

733
00:56:01,250 --> 00:56:03,958
- He sure ain't' jokin'
now, is he, son?
- No, ma'am.

734
00:56:04,020 --> 00:56:06,398
He won't even sit
in the same room
and have a meal today.

735
00:56:06,456 --> 00:56:11,405
Don't make no sense.
Big ox like Grady won't sit
next to a colored child,

736
00:56:11,461 --> 00:56:14,908
but he eats eggs-
Shoot right out
of a chicken's ass.

737
00:56:39,822 --> 00:56:42,496
Come on, Smokey,
let's go for a walk.

738
00:56:51,467 --> 00:56:54,243
I'm sorry about
spillin' my food, ma'am.

739
00:56:54,303 --> 00:56:57,978
I'll just
head on.

740
00:57:06,682 --> 00:57:09,720
See that piece
of land over there?

741
00:57:09,786 --> 00:57:12,596
See it?
That used to be a lake.

742
00:57:12,655 --> 00:57:14,657
Yeah.

743
00:57:14,724 --> 00:57:16,670
This one November,

744
00:57:16,726 --> 00:57:18,672
all these ducks
come by...

745
00:57:18,728 --> 00:57:22,005
and they landed
on that lake.

746
00:57:22,064 --> 00:57:26,171
Then the temperature
dropped so fast, the
whole lake just froze.

747
00:57:26,235 --> 00:57:29,273
Then the ducks
took off and took
the lake with 'em.

748
00:57:29,338 --> 00:57:32,148
Now that lake's somewhere
in Georgia, the way I hear it.

749
00:57:32,208 --> 00:57:34,882
Go on now.

750
00:57:48,491 --> 00:57:50,971
God bless you,
ma'am.

751
00:58:19,956 --> 00:58:22,232
Here, try this.

752
00:58:25,995 --> 00:58:30,034
- So what do you think?
- They're okay.

753
00:58:30,099 --> 00:58:33,808
- The truth.
- Well-

754
00:58:36,405 --> 00:58:39,181
They're terrible.

755
00:58:39,242 --> 00:58:44,191
Oh, well, don't be shy.
Tell me how you feel.

756
00:58:44,247 --> 00:58:46,784
I will.

757
00:58:59,462 --> 00:59:01,635
What'd you go
and do that for?

758
00:59:04,433 --> 00:59:07,710
I just thought you needed
a little coolin' off.

759
00:59:07,770 --> 00:59:11,877
You're right.

760
00:59:25,221 --> 00:59:28,634
Try these.

761
00:59:32,461 --> 00:59:35,135
I think we need
to make a little paste.

762
00:59:54,216 --> 00:59:56,958
What in the name
of Christmas are
you two doing?

763
00:59:57,019 --> 00:59:58,965
She's tryin'
to teach me
how to cook.

764
00:59:59,021 --> 01:00:01,900
Look at those
fried green tomatoes.

765
01:00:05,995 --> 01:00:10,341
You better stop this.
I'm gonna have to arrest you
for disorderly conduct.

766
01:00:10,399 --> 01:00:12,879
Arrest us then.
Let me handle this.

767
01:00:12,935 --> 01:00:15,211
- All right.
- Grady.

768
01:00:17,006 --> 01:00:19,509
Ha-ha-ha!

769
01:00:19,575 --> 01:00:23,751
Arrest us.
Go ahead, arrest us.

770
01:00:23,813 --> 01:00:28,193
Ruth, I have to say it.
I believe Idgie's been
a bad influence on ya.

771
01:00:28,250 --> 01:00:31,390
I agree.

772
01:01:10,393 --> 01:01:13,499
I'll be back in a minute.

773
01:01:13,562 --> 01:01:15,633
Y'all keep the show
going till then.

774
01:01:15,698 --> 01:01:17,735
We ain't goin'
nowhere.

775
01:01:27,284 --> 01:01:31,323
I ain't scared
of you! No, sir!

776
01:01:31,388 --> 01:01:34,801
You should be.

777
01:01:44,535 --> 01:01:46,913
Mind your manners, boy!

778
01:01:55,812 --> 01:01:58,190
Grady,

779
01:01:58,248 --> 01:02:01,491
what does Gladys think
of you stayin' out late...

780
01:02:01,552 --> 01:02:05,864
and losin' your money to me
in poker night after night?

781
01:02:06,690 --> 01:02:09,534
She likes it
just fine.

782
01:02:14,097 --> 01:02:16,737
- They got Big George.
- Idgie!

783
01:02:16,800 --> 01:02:19,303
- Let go of him!
- Let me handle this!

784
01:02:19,369 --> 01:02:23,249
We seen how you treat
your niggers around here
and we don't like it.

785
01:02:23,307 --> 01:02:27,585
I'm the law in these parts.
I don't care what you
like or don't like.

786
01:02:27,644 --> 01:02:29,624
Turn him loose.

787
01:02:29,680 --> 01:02:32,889
Don't get riled up,
nigger lover.

788
01:02:32,950 --> 01:02:37,421
You deaf or somethin'?
I said, let him go!

789
01:02:37,487 --> 01:02:40,468
- Before you get yourselves
in a whole lot of trouble!
- Calm down.

790
01:02:40,524 --> 01:02:43,300
We wanted to have
a little get-together...

791
01:02:43,360 --> 01:02:46,341
and make sure we see
eye to eye on some things.

792
01:02:46,396 --> 01:02:49,843
You hear me now?

793
01:02:49,900 --> 01:02:51,937
Let's let him go, boys.

794
01:02:52,002 --> 01:02:53,709
We've had enough fun
for one night.

795
01:02:53,770 --> 01:02:55,716
- Turn him loose.
- Come on.

796
01:02:55,772 --> 01:02:57,752
No, you're gonna
get in trouble.

797
01:03:00,310 --> 01:03:02,847
Well, now,
that's more like it.

798
01:03:02,913 --> 01:03:05,860
Seems I don't recognize
any of you boys.

799
01:03:05,916 --> 01:03:08,157
Y'all ain't from Whistle Stop,
are you?

800
01:03:11,188 --> 01:03:13,259
This ought to do it.

801
01:03:13,323 --> 01:03:16,327
I want to thank you,
Miss Idgie.

802
01:03:16,393 --> 01:03:21,570
Forget it.
You'd have done
the same for me.

803
01:03:21,632 --> 01:03:25,444
Try to get some sleep.

804
01:03:30,240 --> 01:03:33,346
Who the hell
were those assholes?

805
01:03:33,410 --> 01:03:38,689
They's just some old boys
from Georgia come over here
to put a scare in you.

806
01:03:38,749 --> 01:03:41,195
Well, it worked.

807
01:03:41,251 --> 01:03:43,959
One of 'em was here
the other day for something,

808
01:03:44,021 --> 01:03:46,558
seen you sellin' food
to coloreds.

809
01:03:46,623 --> 01:03:50,696
They decided to come back,
shake you up a bit.

810
01:03:50,761 --> 01:03:54,208
I told 'em we don't need
anybody from Georgia
comin' over here...

811
01:03:54,264 --> 01:03:56,801
tellin' us what
we can or cannot do.

812
01:03:56,867 --> 01:04:02,044
They won't be back.
I guaran-gol-damn-tee
you that.

813
01:04:02,105 --> 01:04:05,177
One other thing,
little Miss Smarty-pants,

814
01:04:05,242 --> 01:04:09,520
I do not wear a size 14 shoe...

815
01:04:09,579 --> 01:04:13,152
and I don't
much care for parades,

816
01:04:13,216 --> 01:04:16,823
bedsheets or otherwise.

817
01:05:00,877 --> 01:05:04,222
- Hey there!
- You got to come quick.

818
01:05:04,280 --> 01:05:07,454
Well, the show
has hardly begun.

819
01:05:07,517 --> 01:05:10,259
You got to come quick now.
You hear me?

820
01:05:12,989 --> 01:05:15,299
- Run, get help!
Run, quick!
- Where's the baby?

821
01:05:15,358 --> 01:05:17,395
Never mind.

822
01:05:36,812 --> 01:05:42,353
Excuse me, sir.
I don't believe you
should be goin' anywhere...

823
01:05:42,418 --> 01:05:44,989
with Ruth's baby.

824
01:06:28,670 --> 01:06:33,449
That's my husband,
but I haven't seen
him in months.

825
01:06:33,508 --> 01:06:36,751
I heard he got run over
by a Brinks armored truck.

826
01:06:36,812 --> 01:06:38,849
What's he done?

827
01:06:38,914 --> 01:06:42,919
Nothin' that we know of.
We're tryin' to find out
what's been did to him.

828
01:06:42,984 --> 01:06:46,488
He told his hired man he was
comin' to see his wife and baby,

829
01:06:46,555 --> 01:06:50,560
but he ain't never
showed up back home.

830
01:06:50,625 --> 01:06:53,333
Hell, I told him
if he showed up in this town,

831
01:06:53,395 --> 01:06:55,534
we'd all have known.

832
01:06:55,597 --> 01:06:58,043
Looks a little sissified
to me.

833
01:06:58,100 --> 01:07:02,105
From what I hear,
most you boys in Georgia...

834
01:07:02,170 --> 01:07:03,615
are a little light
on your feet

835
01:07:03,672 --> 01:07:06,846
That's the way
I heard it.

836
01:07:06,908 --> 01:07:09,047
Could I interest you
in some pie?

837
01:07:09,111 --> 01:07:13,025
No, ma'am, but that
barbecue sure smells good.

838
01:07:13,081 --> 01:07:16,528
Best damn barbecue
in the state of Alabama.

839
01:07:45,747 --> 01:07:48,387
Here you go.
That's your 4th one today.

840
01:07:48,450 --> 01:07:51,294
I swear you're about
to eat up all my barbecue.

841
01:07:51,353 --> 01:07:54,129
Sit down.

842
01:08:05,343 --> 01:08:08,017
You sure you ain't
never seen this man, boy?

843
01:08:08,079 --> 01:08:11,720
Yes, sir, and I already told ya,
I ain't never seen him.

844
01:08:11,783 --> 01:08:14,286
You'd do anything for
Miss Idgie, wouldn't ya, boy?

845
01:08:16,187 --> 01:08:18,133
Yes, sir.

846
01:08:21,359 --> 01:08:24,966
Would ya kill for her?
Did ya kill for her?

847
01:08:32,337 --> 01:08:34,476
No, sir.

848
01:08:34,539 --> 01:08:39,386
Well, now, maybe
one of these days
you'll tell the truth.

849
01:08:41,413 --> 01:08:44,121
Just remember, we hang
lyin' niggers in Georgia...

850
01:08:44,182 --> 01:08:47,163
just as fast as
they do in Alabama.

851
01:08:47,218 --> 01:08:50,995
Yes, sir, I remember.

852
01:09:28,560 --> 01:09:33,009
Sorry.

853
01:09:33,064 --> 01:09:38,013
- What are ya
doin' in here?
- No milk in the house.

854
01:09:38,069 --> 01:09:40,174
Where were you?

855
01:09:43,815 --> 01:09:46,091
No!

856
01:09:52,991 --> 01:09:54,937
You don't believe me.

857
01:09:54,993 --> 01:09:59,567
Right now, I don't know
what to believe.

858
01:10:02,033 --> 01:10:05,344
Believe me when I tell ya
I don't want ya to move out.

859
01:10:30,929 --> 01:10:34,274
Finally.

860
01:10:34,332 --> 01:10:38,075
Thanks, I've been
out here all day.

861
01:11:05,230 --> 01:11:07,642
Excuse me.
I was waiting for that space.

862
01:11:07,699 --> 01:11:12,648
- Yeah? Tough!
- Face it, lady,
we're younger and faster.

863
01:11:33,191 --> 01:11:36,104
Towanda.

864
01:11:39,598 --> 01:11:42,636
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

865
01:11:42,701 --> 01:11:47,616
Yeah!
Whooo!

866
01:11:51,977 --> 01:11:54,457
Towanda!

867
01:11:59,317 --> 01:12:02,127
Yes, ma'am.

868
01:12:02,187 --> 01:12:04,895
Whoooo!

869
01:12:07,892 --> 01:12:11,396
- Help, someone!
- What are you doing?
Are you crazy?

870
01:12:11,463 --> 01:12:16,412
Face it, girls.
I'm older, and I
have more insurance.

871
01:12:25,010 --> 01:12:28,651
I never get mad,
Mrs. Threadgoode.
Never!

872
01:12:28,713 --> 01:12:31,284
The way I was raised
it was bad manners.

873
01:12:31,349 --> 01:12:34,523
Well, I got mad
and it felt terrific.

874
01:12:34,586 --> 01:12:37,897
I felt like I could beat
the shit outta all those punks!

875
01:12:40,964 --> 01:12:43,171
so they'll explode
when you open 'em.

876
01:12:43,233 --> 01:12:47,704
I'll ban all fashion models
who weigh less than 130 pounds.

877
01:12:49,506 --> 01:12:53,079
I'll give half the military
budget to people over 65...

878
01:12:53,143 --> 01:12:55,885
and declare wrinkles
sexually desirable.

879
01:12:55,946 --> 01:13:00,588
Towanda, righter of wrongs,
queen beyond compare!

880
01:13:00,650 --> 01:13:03,961
How many of them
hormones you takin', honey?

881
01:13:19,436 --> 01:13:21,939
what I can't
understand is...

882
01:13:22,005 --> 01:13:25,612
how in the hell
you can hit someone...

883
01:13:25,675 --> 01:13:27,916
six times
by accident.

884
01:13:27,978 --> 01:13:31,016
Oh, Ed, don't make
such a big deal about it.

885
01:13:37,420 --> 01:13:41,960
- What the hell is this?
- A low cholesterol meal.

886
01:13:42,025 --> 01:13:43,971
Happy Valentine's.

887
01:13:47,230 --> 01:13:50,177
My God!
Are you tryin' to kill me?

888
01:13:50,233 --> 01:13:53,510
If I was gonna kill ya,
I'd use my hands.

889
01:14:10,420 --> 01:14:13,026
I'm worried about
my little friend Evelyn.

890
01:14:13,089 --> 01:14:15,660
She said her husband...

891
01:14:15,725 --> 01:14:18,035
will just be watching
his sports on TV...

892
01:14:18,094 --> 01:14:21,268
and she has an urge to hit him
in the head with a baseball bat.

893
01:14:21,331 --> 01:14:24,210
Hell, that
seems normal to me.

894
01:14:24,267 --> 01:14:26,269
- Hi Janeen.
- Mm-hmm

895
01:14:26,336 --> 01:14:28,816
Mrs. Threadgoode, would
you like some crudites?

896
01:14:29,823 --> 01:14:31,166
Mommy! Mommy!

897
01:14:39,332 --> 01:14:41,278
Buddy.

898
01:14:41,334 --> 01:14:43,280
Everybody
outta the way.

899
01:14:43,336 --> 01:14:47,113
Give him here.
Let him go. I've got him.

900
01:14:49,076 --> 01:14:51,283
Come on. You're
gonna be all right.

901
01:14:51,344 --> 01:14:53,688
Open the door!

902
01:14:53,747 --> 01:14:57,820
Put him in the car.
It's all right, honey

903
01:15:19,039 --> 01:15:20,950
I can understand...

904
01:15:21,007 --> 01:15:23,544
having a funeral
for an arm.

905
01:15:23,610 --> 01:15:27,148
I just don't know why
she insists on callin'
him "Stump."?

906
01:15:27,214 --> 01:15:30,218
She say everybody else gonna
be callin' him that...

907
01:15:30,283 --> 01:15:34,390
so we might just as well
be the first.

908
01:15:34,454 --> 01:15:38,630
Okay, ice cream
and cake for everybody.

909
01:15:38,692 --> 01:15:40,501
Go on.

910
01:15:44,765 --> 01:15:48,770
My daddy always used to say
there was a separate God
for children.

911
01:15:52,639 --> 01:15:56,177
The good Lord was watchin'
over stump that day.

912
01:15:57,644 --> 01:16:02,957
this poor, weak woman
with promises of
liquor and money,

913
01:16:03,016 --> 01:16:06,759
and she lost control
of her senses momentarily.

914
01:16:06,820 --> 01:16:09,824
When her husband came back
to get her and take her home,

915
01:16:09,890 --> 01:16:14,532
you and your colored man
murdered him in cold blood.

916
01:16:15,729 --> 01:16:17,333
No, sir.

917
01:16:17,397 --> 01:16:22,676
Well, where were you on the
night of September 30, 1933?

918
01:16:22,736 --> 01:16:25,046
I was at the town hall
doing a show.

919
01:16:25,105 --> 01:16:28,211
- And after that?
- I was at
my mother's house.

920
01:16:28,275 --> 01:16:30,812
Oh, yeah?
Who was with you?

921
01:16:30,877 --> 01:16:35,223
- Just Big George and myself
- What about your mother?
Can she confirm that?

922
01:16:35,282 --> 01:16:37,558
No, sir.
She died a year ago.

923
01:16:37,617 --> 01:16:40,120
I'm sorry to hear that.

924
01:16:40,187 --> 01:16:43,896
But do you expect 12 intelligent
men to believe you,

925
01:16:43,957 --> 01:16:46,597
although one witness is dead and
the other is a colored man,

926
01:16:46,660 --> 01:16:50,073
known to be a worthless,
no-good, lying nigger?

927
01:16:50,130 --> 01:16:52,406
You expect these men
to take your word for it...

928
01:16:52,466 --> 01:16:55,140
just because
you say so?

929
01:16:55,202 --> 01:16:59,742
That's right,
you gump-faced, blown-up,
baboon-assed bastard!

930
01:16:59,806 --> 01:17:03,276
One more outburst
like that...

931
01:17:03,343 --> 01:17:06,847
and I'll hold you
in contempt of court.
You understand?

932
01:17:06,913 --> 01:17:09,723
Yes, sir.

933
01:17:14,897 --> 01:17:16,899
I do.

934
01:17:18,934 --> 01:17:23,178
You have information
about the whereabouts...

935
01:17:23,239 --> 01:17:26,846
of Idgie Threadgoode
and her colored man,
known as Big George,

936
01:17:26,909 --> 01:17:30,686
on the night
of September 30, 1933?

937
01:17:30,746 --> 01:17:32,726
Yes, sir,
I do.

938
01:17:32,782 --> 01:17:35,228
It has been
suggested here...

939
01:17:35,284 --> 01:17:38,754
that she and her colored man
were at her mother's house.

940
01:17:38,821 --> 01:17:43,065
- Can you confirm that?
- No, sir.
That is a lie.

941
01:17:43,125 --> 01:17:45,867
Oh, shit.

942
01:17:45,928 --> 01:17:49,171
It has been my habit
to write all the dates...

943
01:17:49,231 --> 01:17:52,178
Of the activities of
the church in my Bible.

944
01:17:52,234 --> 01:17:56,910
I show that the night
of September 30, 1933...

945
01:17:56,972 --> 01:18:00,010
was the start of our
annual revival...

946
01:18:00,075 --> 01:18:02,851
down at the
Baptist campground.

947
01:18:02,912 --> 01:18:05,017
Sister Threadgoode
was there...

948
01:18:05,080 --> 01:18:09,119
along with her hired man,
George Pullman,

949
01:18:09,185 --> 01:18:13,327
who was in charge of the
barbecue as he has been...

950
01:18:13,389 --> 01:18:16,063
- for the last ten years.
- Objection.

951
01:18:16,125 --> 01:18:20,665
That doesn't mean anything.
Murder could've taken place any
time the next couple of clays.

952
01:18:20,729 --> 01:18:25,769
- Have you ever been to one
of our revivals, sir?
- Well, no.

953
01:18:25,835 --> 01:18:27,906
Do you attend church
regularly, sir?

954
01:18:27,970 --> 01:18:30,177
'Course I do.

955
01:18:30,239 --> 01:18:34,779
Good. Well, maybe if you
attended one of our revivals,

956
01:18:34,844 --> 01:18:37,222
you'd know
they last three days...

957
01:18:37,279 --> 01:18:39,623
and three nights,
Your Honor.

958
01:18:41,884 --> 01:18:44,865
Approach the bench.

959
01:18:44,920 --> 01:18:49,630
Percy, it don't look like
you got a case at all.

960
01:18:52,461 --> 01:18:54,907
Whoo!

961
01:19:01,837 --> 01:19:04,750
See you in church,
Sister?

962
01:19:05,641 --> 01:19:07,882
Reverend.

963
01:19:07,943 --> 01:19:12,255
I can't believe he
actually swore on a Bible.

964
01:19:12,314 --> 01:19:14,260
Well, not really.

965
01:19:14,316 --> 01:19:16,318
If that judge
had looked closer,

966
01:19:16,385 --> 01:19:19,457
he'd have seen it was really
a copy of Moby Dick.

967
01:19:21,490 --> 01:19:25,905
- But why did he do it?
- For the sheer joy of
seeing you in church again...

968
01:19:25,961 --> 01:19:28,805
which I suggested to him
might be your penance.

969
01:19:28,864 --> 01:19:31,504
- You didn't promise him,
did you?
- Yes, ma'am, I did.

970
01:19:31,567 --> 01:19:33,513
And I never
break my word.

971
01:19:33,569 --> 01:19:37,949
If I live 1,000 years,
I will never forgive you.

972
01:19:38,007 --> 01:19:42,183
I don't know what's worse,
church or jail.

973
01:19:53,155 --> 01:19:56,295
There now.
Don't you look pretty?

974
01:19:56,358 --> 01:19:58,497
Oh, yes, honey.

975
01:19:58,561 --> 01:20:03,237
You'll have me
lookin' like Ginger Rogers
before you're done.

976
01:20:03,299 --> 01:20:07,543
Don't let Mr. Dunaway see me.
He's liable to go wild.

977
01:20:35,639 --> 01:20:38,677
Evelyn, what in the hell
are you doing?

978
01:20:38,742 --> 01:20:41,655
I need some light
and air.

979
01:20:41,711 --> 01:20:44,920
Why don't you take
one of your walks
or your jog...

980
01:20:44,981 --> 01:20:48,519
or whatever it is
you do?

981
01:20:48,585 --> 01:20:51,498
There's no dinner
either!

982
01:20:51,554 --> 01:20:56,003
Ed, you have any idea
why I've been goin'
to all these classes?

983
01:20:56,059 --> 01:20:59,597
- No.
- I've been trying to save
our marriage.

984
01:20:59,663 --> 01:21:01,700
What's the point
of my tryin'...

985
01:21:01,765 --> 01:21:06,441
if you're gonna sit on
your butt drinking beer...

986
01:21:06,503 --> 01:21:09,347
and watching baseball,
basketball, football...

987
01:21:09,406 --> 01:21:12,546
bowling and hockey
and golf...

988
01:21:12,609 --> 01:21:16,489
and Challenge
of the Gladiators?

989
01:21:22,185 --> 01:21:26,725
Mrs. Couch, I'm Sue,
Mrs. Otis' daughter-in-law.

990
01:21:26,790 --> 01:21:30,237
How are you?
I've heard about you
from Mrs. Threadgoode.

991
01:21:30,293 --> 01:21:34,002
She is so sweet. She's been
lookin' after my mother-in-law.

992
01:21:34,064 --> 01:21:36,840
Now, how is
Mrs. Otis doin',
by the way?

993
01:21:36,900 --> 01:21:41,371
Much better, thank you.
It takes time getting used
to a strange place.

994
01:21:41,438 --> 01:21:45,477
I'm glad to hear it.
Mrs. Threadgoode's
been anxious to get home.

995
01:21:45,542 --> 01:21:49,752
Mrs. Couch, Mrs. Threadgoode
doesn't have a house anymore.

996
01:21:49,813 --> 01:21:53,283
- They tore
that down.
- What?

997
01:21:53,349 --> 01:21:57,593
They had to.
It was falling apart,
and it was condemned.

998
01:21:57,654 --> 01:22:00,601
Oh, no.

999
01:22:00,657 --> 01:22:04,867
- Does she know that?
- No, well, we didn't see
any point in telling her.

1000
01:22:04,928 --> 01:22:07,431
It would just break her heart,
poor old thing

1001
01:22:07,497 --> 01:22:11,445
But I am so glad
I got a chance to meet you.

1002
01:22:11,501 --> 01:22:14,710
You take care of yourself now.
Bye-bye.

1003
01:23:24,674 --> 01:23:26,984
Oh, Evelyn. hey!

1004
01:23:27,043 --> 01:23:29,523
Hey-

1005
01:23:29,579 --> 01:23:31,957
Do you like
my roses?

1006
01:23:32,015 --> 01:23:35,360
Since I can't get home
to look at my own roses...

1007
01:23:35,418 --> 01:23:37,796
I made myself
a paper garden.

1008
01:23:37,854 --> 01:23:41,358
- Got everything
but the bugs.
- They're lovely.

1009
01:23:41,424 --> 01:23:44,701
- You been here long?
- Happy birthday!

1010
01:23:44,761 --> 01:23:47,264
- Oh!
- I shouldn't
have woken you up.

1011
01:23:47,330 --> 01:23:51,608
'Course you should've.
Don't you never let me sleep
through a visitor's day, honey.

1012
01:23:51,668 --> 01:23:56,413
- I look forward to them all week.
- So do I, Mrs. Threadgoode.

1013
01:23:56,472 --> 01:23:59,817
Oh! I can't believe
you remembered.

1014
01:23:59,876 --> 01:24:04,086
You made me
fried green tomatoes!

1015
01:24:06,516 --> 01:24:08,553
Mmm!
They're delicious.

1016
01:24:08,618 --> 01:24:11,963
- It's your recipe.
Are they cold?
- No.
They're just the way...

1017
01:24:12,021 --> 01:24:16,299
- we used to have 'em
at the Whistle Stop Cafe.
- Mmm!

1018
01:24:16,359 --> 01:24:20,307
You couldn't be sweeter to me
if you was my own daughter.

1019
01:24:20,363 --> 01:24:22,536
Here's your napkin.

1020
01:24:22,599 --> 01:24:24,636
And wait-wait-wait.

1021
01:24:24,701 --> 01:24:27,272
Queen, queen.

1022
01:24:30,440 --> 01:24:34,582
You know,
I don't feel 83.

1023
01:24:34,644 --> 01:24:38,786
It sorta slipped up on me.

1024
01:24:40,884 --> 01:24:44,331
I never expected
to live this long.

1025
01:24:44,387 --> 01:24:49,996
'Course, the Lord takes us home
when he wants us.

1026
01:24:59,002 --> 01:25:02,643
Are you all right?

1027
01:25:02,705 --> 01:25:05,049
I was thinking
about Ruth.

1028
01:25:05,108 --> 01:25:07,918
After the trial
was over,

1029
01:25:07,977 --> 01:25:10,184
Everything went back
to normal...

1030
01:25:10,246 --> 01:25:14,023
till that fall
when Ruth lost her appetite.

1031
01:25:14,083 --> 01:25:16,654
By the time Doc Hadley
looked at her,

1032
01:25:16,719 --> 01:25:20,929
he said the cancer was so bad
she only had a couple of weeks.

1033
01:25:20,990 --> 01:25:23,732
Well, we moved her
to the Threadgoode house...

1034
01:25:23,793 --> 01:25:28,640
and put her downstairs
so she'd be more comfortable.

1035
01:25:28,698 --> 01:25:33,204
Sipsey moved in with her
and never left her side.

1036
01:25:33,269 --> 01:25:35,408
Hold on, baby
I'm right here.

1037
01:25:35,471 --> 01:25:40,147
Idgie just prayed
for a miracle.

1038
01:25:59,429 --> 01:26:02,899
Now, listen to me.

1039
01:26:02,966 --> 01:26:05,503
Make sure he graduates.

1040
01:26:05,568 --> 01:26:09,778
And don't... let him
come to the funeral.

1041
01:26:09,839 --> 01:26:12,513
I don't want him going
through that mess.

1042
01:26:12,575 --> 01:26:15,886
Would you quit talkin'
like that?

1043
01:26:15,945 --> 01:26:18,448
What funeral?

1044
01:26:18,514 --> 01:26:20,892
You're gonna be back on
your feet feelin' just fine...

1045
01:26:20,950 --> 01:26:23,624
in just a few days.

1046
01:26:23,686 --> 01:26:26,599
Just you wait.

1047
01:26:26,656 --> 01:26:29,796
Oh, what's the matter,
son?

1048
01:26:35,631 --> 01:26:39,306
Well,
let's go for a walk.

1049
01:26:40,003 --> 01:26:41,607
Did you get
into a fight?

1050
01:26:41,671 --> 01:26:44,379
I got punched
in the nose.

1051
01:26:44,440 --> 01:26:47,944
I can't play
like everyone else.

1052
01:26:48,011 --> 01:26:51,549
Did I ever tell you the
story about... the oysters?

1053
01:26:51,614 --> 01:26:54,094
All the millions of 'em
just lying around-

1054
01:26:54,150 --> 01:26:58,997
- And God put sand in one of 'em,
and it makes a pearl.
- Oh.

1055
01:27:00,757 --> 01:27:03,431
Did I ever tell you about
Eva's three-legged dog?

1056
01:27:03,493 --> 01:27:05,598
How it never felt sorry
for itself...

1057
01:27:05,661 --> 01:27:09,302
and howl ought to be
smarter than a dumb dog
and not feel sorry for myself.

1058
01:27:11,100 --> 01:27:14,445
You listen to everything
I say, don't you?

1059
01:27:14,504 --> 01:27:17,485
You get real mad at me
when I don't.

1060
01:27:17,540 --> 01:27:19,247
Well,

1061
01:27:21,711 --> 01:27:24,715
you know about
your mama.

1062
01:27:24,781 --> 01:27:27,284
She's sick.

1063
01:27:27,350 --> 01:27:29,387
Mm-hmm.

1064
01:27:30,920 --> 01:27:34,367
See, now is the time
for courage.

1065
01:27:34,424 --> 01:27:38,133
I guess you already know
that there are...

1066
01:27:38,194 --> 01:27:41,198
angels masqueradin' as people
walkin' around this planet,

1067
01:27:41,264 --> 01:27:44,438
and your mom's
the bravest one of those.

1068
01:27:48,704 --> 01:27:50,809
Come here.

1069
01:27:58,514 --> 01:28:00,926
Mama, I can hit!
You should see me.

1070
01:28:00,983 --> 01:28:03,793
Idgie, she hit me in
the back with a curveball.

1071
01:28:03,853 --> 01:28:06,026
I didn't duck,
and I hardly cried.

1072
01:28:06,089 --> 01:28:09,559
She hit you?

1073
01:28:09,625 --> 01:28:13,630
Well, she did that
to me once too,

1074
01:28:13,696 --> 01:28:16,472
but I think
I did cry.

1075
01:28:18,367 --> 01:28:22,338
Mama, I'm sorry
if you're sad.

1076
01:28:22,405 --> 01:28:24,715
Well,

1077
01:28:24,774 --> 01:28:27,880
give me a big kiss then,
and I'll never be sad again.

1078
01:28:35,418 --> 01:28:38,331
And you best not be sad
neither.

1079
01:28:38,387 --> 01:28:41,630
You understand?

1080
01:28:41,691 --> 01:28:43,637
You promise?

1081
01:28:43,693 --> 01:28:45,730
Promise.

1082
01:28:45,795 --> 01:28:49,743
Attaboy.
You go and wash up.

1083
01:29:13,556 --> 01:29:15,593
Sweet baby.

1084
01:29:19,562 --> 01:29:22,839
You two
be alone now.

1085
01:29:23,533 --> 01:29:27,208
Hey, girl.

1086
01:29:29,705 --> 01:29:31,776
No.

1087
01:29:33,709 --> 01:29:36,781
That's nice.

1088
01:29:37,780 --> 01:29:41,489
Will you do one thing
for me?

1089
01:29:41,551 --> 01:29:45,158
- Yeah, anything.
- Be good to yourself.

1090
01:29:45,221 --> 01:29:48,168
Even...

1091
01:29:48,224 --> 01:29:50,761
settle down if
you can find someone...

1092
01:29:50,826 --> 01:29:53,568
who can beat you
in poker.

1093
01:30:01,270 --> 01:30:06,242
There's so many things
I want to say to you.

1094
01:30:06,309 --> 01:30:08,846
No.

1095
01:30:09,679 --> 01:30:12,353
I love your stories.

1096
01:30:12,415 --> 01:30:15,362
Tell me a story,
Idgie.

1097
01:30:18,221 --> 01:30:22,067
Oh, God.

1098
01:30:22,124 --> 01:30:25,230
Go on,
you old' bee charmer.

1099
01:30:25,294 --> 01:30:28,969
Tell me
a good tall tale.

1100
01:30:30,366 --> 01:30:34,075
Tell me the one
about the lake.

1101
01:30:35,371 --> 01:30:40,013
- What lake?
- The one...
that used to be here.

1102
01:30:42,144 --> 01:30:44,090
Oh.

1103
01:30:46,148 --> 01:30:49,721
Well, that was
just a lie.

1104
01:30:49,785 --> 01:30:52,561
I know that, fool.

1105
01:30:52,622 --> 01:30:54,693
Tell me anyway.

1106
01:30:54,757 --> 01:30:58,170
Tell me the story.

1107
01:30:59,729 --> 01:31:03,176
Well...

1108
01:31:05,201 --> 01:31:07,681
one time...

1109
01:31:07,737 --> 01:31:10,547
there was this lake.

1110
01:31:14,977 --> 01:31:19,357
And, uh, it was
right outside of town.

1111
01:31:19,415 --> 01:31:24,865
We used to go
fishin' and swimmin'
and canoein' in it.

1112
01:31:24,920 --> 01:31:28,163
And see,
one November...

1113
01:31:28,224 --> 01:31:30,534
this big ﬂock
of ducks...

1114
01:31:30,593 --> 01:31:35,633
came in and landed
on that lake and, uh,

1115
01:31:35,698 --> 01:31:40,545
and then the temperature
dropped so fast that the
lake just froze right there.

1116
01:31:40,603 --> 01:31:42,879
And the, uh,

1117
01:31:42,938 --> 01:31:46,715
the ducks, they...

1118
01:31:46,776 --> 01:31:50,952
ﬂew off, you see,
and took that lake with 'em.

1119
01:31:51,013 --> 01:31:54,256
And, uh.

1120
01:31:54,317 --> 01:31:59,323
Now they say that lake is
somewhere over in Georgia.

1121
01:31:59,388 --> 01:32:02,460
Can you imagine?

1122
01:33:00,149 --> 01:33:03,426
It's all right,
honey.

1123
01:33:03,486 --> 01:33:06,023
Let her go.

1124
01:33:06,088 --> 01:33:09,467
Let her go.

1125
01:33:09,525 --> 01:33:13,769
You know,
Miss Ruth was a lady.

1126
01:33:13,829 --> 01:33:17,106
And a lady
always knows...

1127
01:33:17,166 --> 01:33:20,170
when to leave.

1128
01:33:25,674 --> 01:33:29,781
When I think on our
departed sister, Ruth Jamison,

1129
01:33:29,845 --> 01:33:32,951
I'm reminded of our
Lord's Sermon on the Mount...

1130
01:33:33,015 --> 01:33:35,495
and how his teachings-

1131
01:33:35,551 --> 01:33:40,000
It's funny how strong
Ruth affected everyone.

1132
01:33:40,055 --> 01:33:43,468
even Smokey Lonesome.

1133
01:33:43,526 --> 01:33:46,200
When he died
a few years back...

1134
01:33:46,262 --> 01:33:48,970
he had one possession
on him,

1135
01:33:49,031 --> 01:33:51,637
A picture of Ruth.

1136
01:33:53,002 --> 01:33:57,109
He was in love with her
from the first time he saw her.

1137
01:33:57,173 --> 01:34:00,052
We all were.

1138
01:34:06,015 --> 01:34:08,495
I shouldn't
a-told you this.

1139
01:34:10,419 --> 01:34:14,390
I hate death.
It scares me so.

1140
01:34:14,457 --> 01:34:16,994
Death is nothin'
to be afraid of!

1141
01:34:17,059 --> 01:34:20,131
Look at me. I'm at
the jumpin'-off place,

1142
01:34:20,196 --> 01:34:23,439
and I ain't afraid
one bit.

1143
01:34:23,499 --> 01:34:27,208
Oh, Ninny,
you're so brave.

1144
01:34:28,771 --> 01:34:32,719
Ruth and Idgie were brave,
not me.

1145
01:34:32,775 --> 01:34:36,154
I wouldn't be afraid
of death if I was you.

1146
01:34:36,212 --> 01:34:41,161
I'd be more afraid of driving
in rush-hour traffic.

1147
01:36:36,365 --> 01:36:39,369
Hi, honey.
Look what I got you.

1148
01:36:39,435 --> 01:36:41,472
Ah...

1149
01:36:41,537 --> 01:36:45,007
Ed, how sweet!

1150
01:36:45,074 --> 01:36:47,520
- Lilies!
My favorite.
- Yeah.

1151
01:36:47,576 --> 01:36:50,716
I know.
Sometimes I even amaze myself.

1152
01:36:50,779 --> 01:36:54,886
- What's the occasion?
- Oh, honey,
I just...

1153
01:36:54,950 --> 01:36:57,931
feel sorry about
the past few months.

1154
01:36:57,987 --> 01:37:01,992
I don't know what
you're really up to and
what's going on with you,

1155
01:37:02,057 --> 01:37:06,472
but I guess I could've been
more helpful with your job
and everything, you know.

1156
01:37:07,696 --> 01:37:09,573
Well, why are you...

1157
01:37:09,632 --> 01:37:12,613
puttin' up this wall
where you just tore one down?

1158
01:37:12,668 --> 01:37:15,808
Well...
I changed my mind.

1159
01:37:15,871 --> 01:37:18,647
I don't mean to seem
dense or anything,

1160
01:37:18,707 --> 01:37:22,951
- but what's changed?
- The air and the light.

1161
01:37:25,314 --> 01:37:27,920
- Ed-
- Hmm?

1162
01:37:27,983 --> 01:37:30,463
You remember how
you used to tell me...

1163
01:37:30,519 --> 01:37:33,261
you always wanted
two women in your house?

1164
01:37:33,322 --> 01:37:35,632
Oh, God.

1165
01:37:35,691 --> 01:37:37,364
Yeah.

1166
01:37:37,426 --> 01:37:39,463
Well...

1167
01:37:39,528 --> 01:37:42,475
what if I was
the younger of the two?

1168
01:37:42,531 --> 01:37:46,069
I don't believe
I get your drift.

1169
01:37:46,135 --> 01:37:50,675
I want something
more than I've ever
wanted anything before.

1170
01:37:50,739 --> 01:37:53,515
I want to bring
Mrs. Threadgoode...

1171
01:37:53,575 --> 01:37:55,782
to our home.

1172
01:37:55,844 --> 01:37:58,484
I want her
to live here with us.

1173
01:37:58,547 --> 01:38:01,050
I want to give her the love
she's given me.

1174
01:38:01,116 --> 01:38:05,292
You're kiddin' me, aren't you?
I'm absolutely serious.

1175
01:38:05,354 --> 01:38:10,201
That's why I'm puttin' the
wall to Kyle's room back up.

1176
01:38:10,259 --> 01:38:13,331
Well, honey, this isn't
something you're just go and do.

1177
01:38:13,395 --> 01:38:16,069
I mean,
she's an old woman.

1178
01:38:16,131 --> 01:38:19,374
What if she got sick?
Who's gonna take care of her?

1179
01:38:19,435 --> 01:38:21,142
I will!

1180
01:38:21,203 --> 01:38:23,205
I can't leave her
in that place.

1181
01:38:23,272 --> 01:38:27,186
She's not a stray cat.
Hell, she isn't even family.

1182
01:38:27,242 --> 01:38:30,314
- She's family to me.
- Now, Evelyn.

1183
01:38:31,146 --> 01:38:34,218
Evelyn?

1184
01:38:34,283 --> 01:38:36,160
Honey?

1185
01:38:36,218 --> 01:38:38,220
Ah, look...

1186
01:38:38,287 --> 01:38:42,531
have you mentioned this
harebrained idea to her?

1187
01:38:42,591 --> 01:38:45,663
- Not yet.
- Well, good!

1188
01:38:45,728 --> 01:38:48,208
Then we'll just pretend
it never happened.

1189
01:38:48,263 --> 01:38:51,301
I'm making my own money.
I'll pay for everything.

1190
01:38:51,366 --> 01:38:54,939
You don't have to do
a thing.

1191
01:38:55,003 --> 01:38:57,506
Evelyn...

1192
01:38:57,573 --> 01:39:00,053
it's never
gonna happen.

1193
01:39:00,109 --> 01:39:02,783
So just forget
about it.

1194
01:39:04,379 --> 01:39:07,155
Don't you ever
say "never" to me.

1195
01:39:16,091 --> 01:39:18,901
Someone helped put a mirror
up in front of my face,

1196
01:39:18,961 --> 01:39:21,567
and I didn't like
what I saw one bit.

1197
01:39:21,630 --> 01:39:25,476
You know what I did?
I changed.

1198
01:39:25,534 --> 01:39:29,448
And that someone...
was Mrs. Threadgoode.

1199
01:39:29,505 --> 01:39:34,011
She needs my love
and care, and I'm
gonna give it to her.

1200
01:39:35,778 --> 01:39:39,419
If you'll excuse me,
I have to go to the gym.

1201
01:39:44,353 --> 01:39:47,391
And if you won't listen
to reason...

1202
01:39:47,456 --> 01:39:51,097
there's always Towanda.

1203
01:40:05,874 --> 01:40:08,855
Hey, Nin-

1204
01:40:11,513 --> 01:40:14,551
What are you doing?

1205
01:40:14,616 --> 01:40:17,358
Those are her things,
Mrs. Threadgoode's things!

1206
01:40:17,419 --> 01:40:20,525
- What are you doing in here?
Where's Mrs. Threadgoode?
- Who?

1207
01:40:20,589 --> 01:40:23,433
Mrs. Threadgoode!
The woman who lives here.
Are you deaf?

1208
01:40:23,492 --> 01:40:26,405
I'm sorry, miss.
All they told me...

1209
01:40:26,461 --> 01:40:30,671
was that the woman who lived
in here died this morning.

1210
01:40:32,534 --> 01:40:34,673
Oh. my God!

1211
01:40:34,736 --> 01:40:39,082
Wha- What
are you sayin'?

1212
01:40:39,141 --> 01:40:41,314
She died early
this morning.

1213
01:40:41,376 --> 01:40:45,722
They were shorthanded
so they asked me to take
all this stuff down.

1214
01:40:45,781 --> 01:40:48,284
That? all I know.

1215
01:41:07,669 --> 01:41:09,615
Stop that!

1216
01:41:09,671 --> 01:41:12,049
What is the matter
with you people?

1217
01:41:12,107 --> 01:41:15,054
Can't you wait a goddamn day,
for Chrissake?

1218
01:41:15,110 --> 01:41:18,114
Do you have no respect?
These are her things!

1219
01:41:18,180 --> 01:41:22,356
I'm sorry, but they told me
to get this room ready
for another patient.

1220
01:41:22,417 --> 01:41:25,626
She may be just
another patient to you,

1221
01:41:25,687 --> 01:41:29,794
- but she was my friend,
and I loved her.
- I'm sorry.

1222
01:41:29,858 --> 01:41:31,804
I'm just
following orders.

1223
01:41:31,860 --> 01:41:34,807
- What is going on?
- Why didn't
you call me?

1224
01:41:34,863 --> 01:41:38,208
- You could've called me before
you sent that idiot-
- I'm sorry.

1225
01:41:38,267 --> 01:41:40,941
It never occurred to me
that you would take it
this hard.

1226
01:41:41,003 --> 01:41:44,644
- I didn't even get
to tell her good-bye.
- Oh, I know.

1227
01:41:44,706 --> 01:41:48,677
These things are difficult,
but she died peacefully
in her sleep.

1228
01:41:48,744 --> 01:41:52,021
To tell you the truth,
I thought you'd be happy
for Mrs. Threadgoode.

1229
01:41:52,080 --> 01:41:55,118
- Happy?
- Why, yes!
This is what she wanted.

1230
01:41:55,183 --> 01:41:57,129
What?
To be dead?

1231
01:41:57,185 --> 01:41:59,722
No, to go home.
You just missed her.

1232
01:41:59,788 --> 01:42:02,234
She left in a yellow cab
about a half hour ago.

1233
01:42:02,291 --> 01:42:04,999
I don't understand.
What? A cab?

1234
01:42:05,060 --> 01:42:09,338
She said there wasn't no
reason for her to stay now
that Mrs. Otis had died.

1235
01:42:09,398 --> 01:42:12,038
Mrs...

1236
01:42:12,100 --> 01:42:14,273
Otis is dead?

1237
01:42:14,336 --> 01:42:18,216
Oh, Mrs. Otis died.

1238
01:42:18,273 --> 01:42:20,275
Mrs. Otis died!

1239
01:42:20,342 --> 01:42:23,551
Mrs. Otis!
Oh, God!

1240
01:42:23,612 --> 01:42:27,651
Not that... I'm glad that
Mrs. Otis died, it's just-

1241
01:42:27,716 --> 01:42:30,356
Oh, God.
I've gotta stop her.

1242
01:43:09,791 --> 01:43:13,034
Hey, Evelyn,
somebody stole my house.

1243
01:43:13,095 --> 01:43:16,008
It was right here
when I left.

1244
01:43:16,064 --> 01:43:20,843
Unless- Oh, Evelyn,
you don't reckon
I'm crazy, do you?

1245
01:43:20,902 --> 01:43:25,112
- It was here
when I left.
- No, honey,
you're not crazy.

1246
01:43:25,173 --> 01:43:27,949
This is the place.

1247
01:43:28,010 --> 01:43:32,049
Why would anyone want to
steal an old lady's home?

1248
01:43:32,114 --> 01:43:34,253
Wasn't worth nothin'.

1249
01:43:34,316 --> 01:43:37,729
Oh, honey,
nobody stole it.

1250
01:43:37,786 --> 01:43:41,666
They had to tear it down.
It was condemned.

1251
01:43:41,723 --> 01:43:43,862
I'm sorry.
I shoulda told you.

1252
01:43:43,925 --> 01:43:47,202
Well, somebody
shoulda told me.

1253
01:43:47,262 --> 01:43:52,109
- I'm old.
I'm not a child.
- I'm sorry.

1254
01:43:52,167 --> 01:43:55,512
My husband Cleo and I
lived in this house...

1255
01:43:55,570 --> 01:43:58,073
for more than 40 years.

1256
01:43:58,140 --> 01:44:01,553
Now, it's... it's gone.

1257
01:44:01,610 --> 01:44:05,183
83 years worth of livin'
and all that's left of me...

1258
01:44:05,247 --> 01:44:09,286
is what's in this box, a
bunch of old cards and pictures.

1259
01:44:09,351 --> 01:44:11,831
Come on.
I'll take you home.

1260
01:44:11,887 --> 01:44:14,026
This is my home!

1261
01:44:14,089 --> 01:44:16,091
And now it's gone.

1262
01:44:16,158 --> 01:44:18,695
And Mrs. Otis
is gone.

1263
01:44:18,760 --> 01:44:20,865
I...

1264
01:44:20,929 --> 01:44:23,535
I don't quite
know what to do.

1265
01:44:23,598 --> 01:44:27,444
This is the first time
I can remember when I don't
have a soul to look after.

1266
01:44:27,502 --> 01:44:29,880
You can come
look after me and Ed.

1267
01:44:29,938 --> 01:44:32,248
Oh, you're sweet,

1268
01:44:32,307 --> 01:44:35,117
but I think you're doin'
just fine on your own.

1269
01:44:35,177 --> 01:44:39,489
Don't you know you'd be
like a gift for us?

1270
01:44:39,548 --> 01:44:42,722
You're the reason
I get up every morning...

1271
01:44:42,784 --> 01:44:46,129
and that Mary Kay's
havin' such a good year...

1272
01:44:46,188 --> 01:44:50,762
and I don't look like some
blob from a horror movie.

1273
01:44:50,826 --> 01:44:54,865
Well,with a little help
from Idgie and Ruth.

1274
01:44:56,431 --> 01:44:58,968
Come on. I've got
your room all ready.

1275
01:44:59,034 --> 01:45:01,446
What does Ed say
about all this?

1276
01:45:01,503 --> 01:45:05,349
He'll learn
to love it.

1277
01:45:08,810 --> 01:45:12,952
Did I ever tell you
that Mrs. Otis was
Sipsey's baby sister?

1278
01:45:13,014 --> 01:45:15,688
- No, ma'am.
- Yes, she was.

1279
01:45:15,750 --> 01:45:19,630
Mrs. Otis was with
Sipsey and me the
night Sipsey died.

1280
01:45:44,692 --> 01:45:48,230
- Hey there!
- You got to come quick.

1281
01:45:48,296 --> 01:45:53,268
- The show has hardly begun.
- You got to come quick.
You hear me?

1282
01:45:59,173 --> 01:46:01,779
- Run, get help!
Run, quick!
- Where's the baby?

1283
01:46:01,843 --> 01:46:03,652
Never mind.

1284
01:46:22,363 --> 01:46:24,036
Excuse me, sir.

1285
01:46:24,098 --> 01:46:29,605
I don't believe you
should be goin' anywhere
with Ruth's baby.

1286
01:46:41,249 --> 01:46:43,991
Like I said,
you ain't goin' nowhere.

1287
01:46:44,051 --> 01:46:46,622
Damn, you a thickheaded
son-of-a-bitch, ain't you?

1288
01:46:50,825 --> 01:46:52,805
I told you...

1289
01:46:52,860 --> 01:46:57,309
you ain't goin' nowheres
with Miss Ruth's baby.

1290
01:47:02,937 --> 01:47:05,144
Come on, angel.
Come on.

1291
01:47:05,206 --> 01:47:09,052
Come on, sweetheart.
It's all right.

1292
01:47:09,110 --> 01:47:11,613
Come on.
It's all right, baby.

1293
01:47:14,515 --> 01:47:17,257
it was self-defense.

1294
01:47:17,318 --> 01:47:22,165
I don't know why any
white jury would care
why I did it.

1295
01:47:22,223 --> 01:47:25,033
- Well, I saw it,
and I can testify.
- Excuse me here.

1296
01:47:25,092 --> 01:47:27,265
I don't mean
no offense here,

1297
01:47:27,328 --> 01:47:30,400
but I don't know who's less
likely to convince a jury,

1298
01:47:30,464 --> 01:47:32,740
my mama...
or Mr. Smokey.

1299
01:47:32,800 --> 01:47:35,610
No offense taken.

1300
01:47:35,670 --> 01:47:38,082
You're a good man,
Mr. Smokey.

1301
01:47:38,139 --> 01:47:42,178
- You did good.
- The sun's almost up.

1302
01:47:45,713 --> 01:47:49,092
- George?
- Mm-hmm?

1303
01:47:49,150 --> 01:47:51,926
I think...

1304
01:47:51,986 --> 01:47:55,524
it's hog-boiling time.

1305
01:47:55,589 --> 01:47:57,865
No, ma'am. It
ain't cold enough.

1306
01:47:57,925 --> 01:48:00,701
It's hog-boiling time.

1307
01:48:03,631 --> 01:48:05,577
Big George?

1308
01:48:05,633 --> 01:48:08,739
- Uh-huh?
- When is that barbecue
gonna be ready?

1309
01:48:08,803 --> 01:48:11,147
It's gonna be ready
any time now.

1310
01:48:11,205 --> 01:48:16,120
Smells so damn good I just
can't wait to get me some.

1311
01:48:16,177 --> 01:48:20,489
- Now, don't you forget
to call me when that's ready.
- All right.

1312
01:48:34,228 --> 01:48:36,504
Here you go.

1313
01:48:38,065 --> 01:48:41,706
- Miss Idgie?
Smokey left town.
- Yeah?

1314
01:48:41,769 --> 01:48:45,774
I thought it'd be best
under the circumstances.

1315
01:48:45,840 --> 01:48:49,811
He asked that
you tell Ruth good-bye.

1316
01:48:49,877 --> 01:48:52,357
Shame he had to go.

1317
01:48:59,320 --> 01:49:04,235
Hold on! I'm comin'.

1318
01:49:09,096 --> 01:49:11,872
- What you want?
- We want some barbecue.

1319
01:49:11,932 --> 01:49:15,641
Not today you don't.
Go on.

1320
01:49:28,682 --> 01:49:31,822
Why, this is about the
best barbecue I ever ate!

1321
01:49:33,320 --> 01:49:36,824
The secret's
in the sauce.

1322
01:49:48,049 --> 01:49:51,360
I feel better 'cause
all these people'll live...

1323
01:49:51,419 --> 01:49:54,491
as long as
you remember 'em.

1324
01:49:54,556 --> 01:49:56,502
You reminded me...

1325
01:49:56,558 --> 01:49:59,971
about what the most
important thing in life is.

1326
01:50:00,028 --> 01:50:02,372
- Do you know
what I think it is?
- No, ma'am.

1327
01:50:02,430 --> 01:50:05,707
Friends.
Best friends.

1328
01:50:05,767 --> 01:50:08,805
Oh. Ninny!

1329
01:50:09,971 --> 01:50:11,712
Look.

1330
01:50:16,978 --> 01:50:18,821
Oh!

1331
01:50:38,032 --> 01:50:39,978
Idgie?

1332
01:50:43,438 --> 01:50:47,318
- Idgie's alive?
- Oh, yes!

1333
01:50:47,375 --> 01:50:51,653
She's still out and about
Charmin' bees and selling honey.

1334
01:50:51,713 --> 01:50:55,684
Sometimes I think
I catch a glimpse of her.

1335
01:51:01,589 --> 01:51:04,035
Maybe we'll
see her today.

1336
01:51:04,092 --> 01:51:06,732
Maybe.

1337
01:51:08,396 --> 01:51:11,104
Let's go.

1338
01:51:22,610 --> 01:51:26,922
After Ruth died and
the railroad stopped runnin',

1339
01:51:26,981 --> 01:51:30,986
the cafe shut down, and everybody
just scattered to the winds.

1340
01:51:32,320 --> 01:51:35,699
It was never more than just
a little knockabout place.

1341
01:51:35,757 --> 01:51:38,567
But now that
I look back on it,

1342
01:51:38,626 --> 01:51:40,902
when that cafe closed...

1343
01:51:40,962 --> 01:51:45,069
the heart of the town
just stopped beating.

1344
01:51:45,133 --> 01:51:47,977
It's funny how
a little place like this...

1345
01:51:48,036 --> 01:51:51,882
brought so
